Before obtaining an SSL certificate, ensure:

Domain Name: You need a registered domain name (or a free DNS hostname like DuckDNS or No-IP) pointing to your EC2 public IP.


AWS Security Group Rules: In your AWS EC2 Console, ensure both Port 80 (HTTP) and Port 443 (HTTPS) are open to the world (0.0.0.0/0).


Host Firewall (UFW): Open ports 80 and 443 on your server:

sudo ufw allow 80/tcp comment 'HTTP Web Ingress'
sudo ufw allow 443/tcp comment 'HTTPS Encrypted Ingress'
sudo ufw reload







